<http://data.silknow.org/object/a92456aa-534a-3e72-826a-0c2eb1cbce23>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Fragment of shroud believed to have been part of the shroud of a bishop of Burgo de Osma. Design of pairs of lions attacking human-headed birds within circles connected by smaller circles containing inscriptions, woven with red, green, and light brown silk (weft) and gold thread (brocaded). The inscription has been translated by R. Guest as follows \"This was made in the town of Baghdad, may God guard it.\""@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/97873555-8ab2-347d-800c-2d19bf314dd3> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/b9bb2320-0dc8-3f1f-8cb4-f2dc5be79fa5> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/8b4153c4-7348-3dec-b298-3cf159d23a87> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Fragment of shroud believed to have been part of the shroud of a bishop of Burgo de Osma. Design of pairs of lions attacking human-headed birds within circles connected by smaller circles containing inscriptions, woven with red, green, and light brown silk (weft) and gold thread (brocaded). The inscription has been translated by R. Guest as follows \"This was made in the town of Baghdad, may God guard it.\""@en ;
